WEBVTT

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:09.050
What did that last speech mean?

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:11.190
I'm not sure, but...

00:00:11.190 --> 00:00:13.050
A civil war?

00:00:13.050 --> 00:00:15.130
What's happening?

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:20.430
Basically, the brass was planning on making peace with Ingelmia.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:25.140
But Brigadier General Cayenne opposed this, and is saying he'll fight to the end.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:26.360
That's what's going on.

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:30.630
Does that mean we just continue what we've been doing?

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.810
So we resist to the end. That's good, isn't it?

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:35.150
You taking Cayenne's side, bro?

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:38.240
N-No, that's not it...

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:40.660
I'd prefer peace.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.700
Yeah, it's better than war.

00:00:43.700 --> 00:00:46.470
But the chief said that making peace when you're losing

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:49.500
basically means you're surrendering.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.850
He said the enemy will take advantage of it.

00:00:51.850 --> 00:00:54.170
That's... complicated.

00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:59.080
Colonel Izumi, I've been waiting for your call.

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:00.180
Where are you now?

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:02.610
A Kurazu supply base.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.730
I listened to Cayenne's speech on the way.

00:01:05.730 --> 00:01:07.320
I see.

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:09.310
Colonel, that speech...

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:12.550
Cayenne was about to be arrested.

00:01:12.550 --> 00:01:15.130
He's just struggling in vain.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:17.530
That's what the brass thinks, anyway.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:20.820
Even so, won't there be a sizable effect?

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.210
Yes.

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:24.270
He'd been preparing for this in advance.

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:27.830
The northwestern base has been all but taken over by his followers.

00:01:27.830 --> 00:01:32.870
We've got friendlies fighting each other near the surrounding bases, too.

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:35.620
A surprising amount of soldiers are supporting Cayenne.

00:01:36.380 --> 00:01:37.710
Samonji is one of them.

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:41.840
What is he doing now?

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.290
Heading to Zianxec.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.680
He'll head to the front lines from there.

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:50.730
He's going to turn around the war like Cayenne said.

00:01:50.730 --> 00:01:52.360
Turn around the war?

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:54.900
No matter how strong the Perfevollens are,

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:56.610
he can't do it with just them...

00:01:56.610 --> 00:01:59.030
It'll be difficult.

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:00.740
That's why I want to ask this of you.

00:02:02.430 --> 00:02:06.410
Destroy the Perfevollen squad in Zianxec.

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:09.250
Only the 8th Unit can do it.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:02.110
Cayenne!

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.530
What are you thinking, you bastard?

00:04:04.890 --> 00:04:08.530
That speech of yours was treason!

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:09.570
I'm well aware.

00:04:09.570 --> 00:04:11.870
Capture
I'm well aware.

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:14.500
Whether it's rebellion or not, I'm doing my job.
Capture

00:04:14.500 --> 00:04:16.130
Whether it's rebellion or not, I'm doing my job.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:17.410
You should know this!

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:20.920
The people don't want to continue the war!

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:23.330
Kageyama-san,

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:26.830
you don't actually believe that there's any one thing

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:28.930
called "the will of the people," do you?

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:34.450
Each individual has his own will.

00:04:34.450 --> 00:04:37.440
And you think you have the power to lead them?

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:40.510
Who knows...

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.440
There are various kinds of power.

00:04:43.730 --> 00:04:46.210
Stop pretending to be a hero.

00:04:50.690 --> 00:04:53.450
Good work. You were fast.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:56.330
Thank you, Brigadier General Cayenne!

00:04:56.700 --> 00:04:59.700
Arrest them where they stand.

00:04:59.700 --> 00:05:01.630
There's something I want to show them later.

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:02.420
Yes, sir!

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:05.560
Damn you, Cayenne!

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:07.280
You won't get away with this!

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:08.710
Don't make a fuss.

00:05:08.710 --> 00:05:10.840
We've already taken measures.

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:11.710
Yes.

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:28.320
Unmanned enemy mech sighted in the Zianxec plains.

00:05:28.320 --> 00:05:30.730
We've begun combat.

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:32.070
Shall we send Sturm Beta?

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:35.130
Lt. Colonel?

00:05:35.130 --> 00:05:38.080
No. This seems a little too good to be true.

00:05:38.390 --> 00:05:39.580
But,

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:42.680
there are no signs of ambush or other suspicious activity in the area.

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:46.090
Yeah.

00:05:49.580 --> 00:05:51.010
Can we do it?

00:05:51.010 --> 00:05:52.140
Do what?

00:05:52.490 --> 00:05:56.670
Well, Captain Samonji's Perfevollens are basically

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:59.380
an unmanned version of Argevollen, right?

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:01.520
And a lot of them.

00:06:01.910 --> 00:06:03.770
Can we stop them by ourselves?

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:05.730
Isn't that too much?

00:06:06.210 --> 00:06:10.720
More than anything, the idea of fighting Captain Samonji is...

00:06:11.700 --> 00:06:13.740
You don't like it?

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:16.960
Am I wrong?

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:18.990
You can't punish a man for thinking.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:22.000
I see it a little differently.

00:06:22.400 --> 00:06:26.810
We can appeal to Captain Samonji's emotions.

00:06:26.810 --> 00:06:29.640
That's what this order means.

00:06:29.640 --> 00:06:32.430
You're a real romanticist.

00:06:34.180 --> 00:06:37.220
It'd be best if we could somehow do that,

00:06:37.220 --> 00:06:40.430
but he's not really the emotional type.

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:44.220
Hey, Tokimune.

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:45.350
What?

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:47.480
Are you sure there aren't any problems?

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:50.080
Yeah. Arge's in perfect shape.

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.490
Ah, um, not that...

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:56.940
I'm a little worried, I guess...

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:01.370
You have a lot of complicated feelings towards Captain Samonji, right?

00:07:03.000 --> 00:07:05.660
I don't intend to pry or anything, but...

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:11.760
As it is, you get unstable when you're piloting Arge, don't you?

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:14.040
So I'm worried...

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:16.390
As your partner.

00:07:16.690 --> 00:07:18.190
I see.

00:07:18.190 --> 00:07:20.350
But I think it'll be okay.

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:21.850
I see.

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:25.600
Because you'll be here for me, Jamie.

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:31.680
I told you I heard your voice during combat.

00:07:31.680 --> 00:07:34.610
It was really reassuring to me.

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:36.610
R-Really?

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:39.120
Um, should I recalibrate the

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:41.870
arm area while I've got the chance?

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:43.430
Sure, thanks.

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:45.490
Hang on a second.

00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:49.030
Should we tell them we can hear them?

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:50.880
It's a little too late, I think.

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:54.210
Sheesh, what are they doing on an open line?

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:56.680
It's cute how awkward they are.

00:07:56.680 --> 00:07:59.510
It's good that they're getting along.

00:07:59.510 --> 00:08:00.890
It is not.

00:08:00.890 --> 00:08:03.140
At least do it on a closed line.

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:06.120
By the way, this is a closed line...

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:06.890
Wai—

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:09.030
I'll get started.

00:08:09.030 --> 00:08:10.190
Okay.

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:20.200
This is Seeker.

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:23.080
Perfevollen squad sighted at Zianxec plains.

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:26.560
It's fighting Ingelmia's new models.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:28.580
Ingelmia? You're sure?

00:08:28.580 --> 00:08:29.870
Yes.

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:32.200
It appears they were ambushed.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:33.350
Understood.

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:35.590
Keep me informed.

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:42.720
Attention all units.

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:48.050
Friendly allied mechs are in combat with the enemy.

00:08:48.050 --> 00:08:52.320
As an emergency measure, we will aid the unmanned mechs.

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:54.860
We don't have to fight Captain Samonji?

00:08:55.220 --> 00:08:59.610
Silfy, Lorenz, Tokimune, and Namie are to get ready to roll out.

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:01.050
Have two Sekiei on standby.

00:09:01.760 --> 00:09:03.870
Tokimune Susumu. Roger.

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:33.980
Why?

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:39.610
Why don't they fall back even when they're losing so badly?

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:42.870
You think they're planning something?

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:46.740
I don't know what it is, but...

00:09:47.380 --> 00:09:49.200
The enemy is waiting for something.

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:23.070
Is that him?

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:25.650
LAM Signal online.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.790
He's using Sturm Beta as a shield?

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:40.340
Issue a retreat order!

00:10:40.930 --> 00:10:41.590
What?

00:10:41.590 --> 00:10:42.720
Get them out of there!

00:10:45.600 --> 00:10:47.720
Activate Fascinator.

00:11:00.150 --> 00:11:01.070
What?

00:11:16.990 --> 00:11:18.420
The new models...

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:21.670
...have all shut down?

00:11:27.020 --> 00:11:28.980
"Look at me"?

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:29.680
Who's "me?"

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:47.810
We have taken control of all functions of Sturm Beta.

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:51.990
We will be operating them without life support.

00:11:51.990 --> 00:11:54.570
If you continue to pilot them, we cannot guarantee your safety.

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.300
Damn it! What's going on?

00:12:08.650 --> 00:12:11.210
Tokimune Susumu, get out.

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:13.760
What did you do, Captain?

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:19.260
What did you do to Arge?!

00:12:20.030 --> 00:12:22.770
If you'll just get out, there won't be any casualties.

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:25.770
I won't.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:29.560
I won't leave Arge!

00:12:29.560 --> 00:12:31.510
I promised Jamie.

00:12:31.510 --> 00:12:33.900
This belongs to her and me!

00:12:40.730 --> 00:12:41.870
Senpai!

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:57.550
Captain, you'd kill your own men?

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:02.280
What is it you want to do?

00:13:02.280 --> 00:13:05.180
What is it that's so important that you'd kill your own men?

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:09.730
You can do what you want,

00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:13.190
but at least give the people who trusted you an explanation they can accept!

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:18.950
I'll say it again.

00:13:18.950 --> 00:13:19.700
Get out.

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:24.200
Get out, Private Susumu.

00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:26.770
No matter what he wants,

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:30.960
there's no need for you to risk your life for that thing.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:33.030
So get out.

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:35.960
Get out!

00:13:49.240 --> 00:13:51.190
Forget about Argevollen.

00:13:52.990 --> 00:13:54.420
Survive.

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.240
Do you know what happened?

00:14:04.240 --> 00:14:05.480
Huh?

00:14:05.480 --> 00:14:08.850
Um, not specifically,

00:14:08.850 --> 00:14:11.600
but there was no error display on the panel,

00:14:11.600 --> 00:14:15.810
so this function may have been implemented from the start.

00:14:15.810 --> 00:14:17.080
You're right.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:19.260
From the very start.

00:14:25.870 --> 00:14:29.410
Sergeant Tanita, go recover the Seiran 3.

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:30.390
Roger.

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:43.520
So as long as he has Arge, he doesn't care about the rest?

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:47.430
Tokimune.

00:14:49.790 --> 00:14:51.410
Hey, Tokimune. Are you okay?

00:14:55.200 --> 00:14:56.800
They were all captured?

00:14:56.800 --> 00:14:58.300
We're talking about Sturm Beta!

00:14:58.300 --> 00:15:01.480
That's what the pilots who escaped said.

00:15:02.530 --> 00:15:03.550
Lt. Colonel...

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:11.560
Jamie,

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:12.970
are you okay?

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:14.750
Huh? Oh... Yeah.

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:17.690
Koshy said he'd take Tokimune back.

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:19.690
They say Namie-chan is fine, too.

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:20.980
I see.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.400
Thank goodness.

00:15:23.100 --> 00:15:25.620
Good work, Lieutenant Suzushiro.

00:15:25.620 --> 00:15:27.280
Argevollen was stolen.

00:15:27.690 --> 00:15:29.170
I see.

00:15:29.170 --> 00:15:31.410
But the pilot was safe, right?

00:15:31.410 --> 00:15:32.790
Yes.

00:15:32.790 --> 00:15:34.290
That's what's important.

00:15:34.290 --> 00:15:36.730
I'm sorry for giving you an impossible order.

00:15:36.730 --> 00:15:40.430
Return to the northwestern base and regroup.

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.930
Colonel Izumi, did you know about this?

00:15:52.480 --> 00:15:54.940
I see. I'm glad I asked.

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:01.440
I want to be a good friend to him.

00:16:04.510 --> 00:16:06.670
A man's friendship, huh?

00:16:06.670 --> 00:16:08.450
I can't understand that.

00:16:09.470 --> 00:16:11.660
Return to the northwestern base.

00:16:11.660 --> 00:16:12.870
Understood.

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:18.590
We're leaving?

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:20.460
Yes.

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:23.340
The 8th Unit is returning to the northwestern base.

00:16:23.340 --> 00:16:26.540
Um, I've been thinking about this.

00:16:26.540 --> 00:16:28.540
If this function was implemented from the start,

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:30.720
there must be a way to release it.

00:16:31.160 --> 00:16:33.980
I'll hurry and find it, so let me follow Argevollen—

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:35.350
I can't do that.

00:16:36.940 --> 00:16:39.310
Doesn't this bother you, Suzushiro-san?

00:16:39.310 --> 00:16:42.110
You trusted Samonji-san, and look what he did to you!

00:16:44.900 --> 00:16:46.860
This may be for the best.

00:16:48.590 --> 00:16:52.620
You were worried about Private Susumu's health, weren't you?

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:59.630
Now he won't be killed by Argevollen.

00:17:03.060 --> 00:17:05.430
Corporal Terai, once everybody comes back,

00:17:05.430 --> 00:17:07.610
tell them to head to the northwestern base.

00:17:07.610 --> 00:17:09.320
R-Right.

00:17:09.320 --> 00:17:12.560
But shouldn't you tell them personally?

00:17:13.030 --> 00:17:16.690
The northwestern base may still be in a state of disarray.

00:17:16.690 --> 00:17:19.270
Tell Sergeant Tanita to be careful.

00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:24.190
Suzushiro-san?

00:17:28.310 --> 00:17:30.550
We're heading back to the base right away.

00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:32.200
Huh? For real?

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:47.180
Jamie, what are you doing?

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:49.510
I just don't know anymore...

00:17:49.870 --> 00:17:52.810
Suzushiro-san may be right.

00:17:52.810 --> 00:17:55.120
If it means you'll survive,

00:17:55.120 --> 00:17:57.420
it would be better for Arge to be gone—

00:17:57.420 --> 00:17:58.350
Why?

00:17:59.550 --> 00:18:01.690
Why does he get to decide if someone else lives or dies?

00:18:03.240 --> 00:18:05.450
He wants me to forget about Arge and survive...

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:09.700
But I don't want his help!

00:18:12.010 --> 00:18:14.690
I'm not piloting Arge so I can die!

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:17.200
Why do I have to hear that from him?

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.610
I decided for myself!

00:18:18.610 --> 00:18:21.730
I decided I'd pilot Arge!

00:18:21.730 --> 00:18:23.210
That was my decision.

00:18:23.210 --> 00:18:25.310
And it took me a long time to make it!

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:27.210
He doesn't understand anything!

00:18:27.210 --> 00:18:31.220
How the hell is he even going to maintain it without you, Jamie?

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:33.720
He doesn't understand at all!

00:18:41.120 --> 00:18:42.230
What?

00:18:42.230 --> 00:18:44.860
Nothing, I just remembered something.

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:46.730
That you're an idiot.

00:18:48.610 --> 00:18:50.690
And you're right.

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:52.360
I decided for myself, too.

00:18:53.850 --> 00:18:56.120
That I'd pilot Arge with you.

00:18:58.400 --> 00:19:02.370
I'll tell Suzushiro-san that I'm going to take Arge back from him.

00:19:02.640 --> 00:19:04.880
Suzushiro-san is...

00:19:09.370 --> 00:19:11.040
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:19:13.470 --> 00:19:14.760
Captain Suzushiro!

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:17.770
Please, Captain!

00:19:17.770 --> 00:19:20.300
Let me follow Argevollen!

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:22.910
Me, too! I want to do the same!

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:24.270
Please!

00:19:25.930 --> 00:19:28.330
Private Susumu, Hazaford-san.

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:29.890
You heard your orders.

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:31.590
Head to the northwestern base right—

00:19:43.790 --> 00:19:45.410
We ask you, too!

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:48.530
This time, I'm agreeing with Tokimune!

00:19:48.530 --> 00:19:51.450
I don't want it to end like this!

00:19:51.450 --> 00:19:55.160
I won't feel better until I punch Captain Samonji in the face!

00:19:55.160 --> 00:19:56.640
Let me go!

00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:02.430
Sorry. I didn't do the best job of commanding them.

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:07.270
As you can see, I can't command this unit.

00:20:07.270 --> 00:20:10.620
Normally it would be my job to stop them,

00:20:10.620 --> 00:20:14.130
but I'm not capable of ignoring one of my men being shot.

00:20:14.130 --> 00:20:19.030
I find myself actually liking this kind of situation.

00:20:19.030 --> 00:20:21.610
We, too, uh...

00:20:21.610 --> 00:20:23.950
We're mechanics, but...

00:20:23.950 --> 00:20:27.800
But we know how much it hurts to have a machine you worked on stolen!

00:20:27.800 --> 00:20:29.040
Please!

00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:34.260
What about you, Chief?

00:20:34.260 --> 00:20:37.890
I've never really chased after anything in my whole life.

00:20:37.890 --> 00:20:41.060
But I suppose I could do it once before I died.

00:20:41.470 --> 00:20:43.060
Um...

00:20:43.520 --> 00:20:45.370
Seeker-san just sent a message

00:20:45.370 --> 00:20:49.450
that he was continuing to tail the Perfevollen unit.

00:20:49.450 --> 00:20:54.170
And I think it would be more like the 8th Unit to chase after him!

00:20:54.170 --> 00:20:58.320
I want to support Tokimune-senpai and Jamie-san.

00:20:59.450 --> 00:21:01.330
A-Anyway,

00:21:01.330 --> 00:21:04.290
that's how it is, so...

00:21:04.290 --> 00:21:05.530
Please!

00:21:18.420 --> 00:21:22.100
What I'm about to tell you to do is against orders.

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:24.850
You may no longer be able to remain soldiers.

00:21:36.110 --> 00:21:39.890
The 8th Unit is going to go recover Argevollen.

00:21:39.890 --> 00:21:42.360
We'll stop the advance of the Perfevollens,

00:21:42.360 --> 00:21:45.550
and stop Captain Samonji.

00:21:45.550 --> 00:21:47.330
Are you all ready to go?

00:21:47.330 --> 00:21:48.500
Yes.

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:51.890
Okay, let's go punch the captain!

00:21:51.890 --> 00:21:54.500
That's what we do, after all.

00:22:00.620 --> 00:22:13.920
We gaze into each other's eyes, open our hearts.

00:22:13.920 --> 00:22:20.140
A cycle of strength and weakness.

00:22:20.140 --> 00:22:26.770
Your eyes must have adjusted somewhat.

00:22:26.770 --> 00:22:33.440
Verbalize though I may,

00:22:33.440 --> 00:22:41.240
I remember that I can't

00:22:41.240 --> 00:22:47.870
rationalize everything

00:22:47.870 --> 00:22:55.050
The world will change, as long as I remain courageous.

00:22:56.300 --> 00:23:03.050
The telepathy I wouldn't have discovered alone,

00:23:03.050 --> 00:23:09.180
leads me ahead, behind your dazzling silouette.

00:23:09.180 --> 00:23:16.570
But even so, I'll keep my unwavering gaze on you;

00:23:16.570 --> 00:23:23.160
It'll reach you someday.
